WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.100
He does whatever a Spider can - but what about
body-swapping?

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.040
In an interview with Comics Explained, Spider-Man
actor Tom Holland revealed that he would love

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.520
for Peter Parker and Wolverine to team up
for a body swap movie.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.020
Comics Explained asked Holland which Marvel
movie world outside of the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:21.779
Universe he would like to appear in, and Holland
had his answer at the ready, citing a 15-year-old

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.400
Ultimate Spider-Man storyline.

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:27.860
"Wolverine wakes up in Peter Parker's body,
and he, like, goes to school and all of a

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:31.890
sudden Peter Parker's like being this really
gross, rude man and he like starts hitting

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.200
on the school teacher and stuff."

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.180
Holland's Spider-Man: Far From Home co-star
Zendaya, who plays Michelle "MJ" Jones in

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.700
the current Spider-Man film series, was keen
on the idea.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:45.000
"I would love to see Hugh Jackman try to be
Peter Parker!"

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:47.580
"What is that?

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.020
What are you doing?"

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.740
'He's doing his Wolverine thing."

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:51.420
"Yeah."

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.580
For those unfamiliar with Ultimate Spider-Man,
the issues Holland is referring to are Ultimate

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.240
Spider-Man #66 and #67 from 2004.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:05.120
The story was also loosely adapted into an
episode of Disney XD's Ultimate Spider-Man

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.860
cartoon series in 2012.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.080
“This mask smells."

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.040
"You complete me."

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.720
Issue #66 sees Peter Parker and the powerful
mutant Wolverine coming together after a "bizarre

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.420
occurrence" ties them to each other.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.580
The two heroes try to decode the mystery,
and all the while their personal lives begin

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:23.320
to unravel.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:30.060
Together, #66 and #67 tell a classic Freaky
Friday-type body swap tale; or, as Marvel's

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.351
official description of #67 puts it,

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.380
"Wolverine and Spider-Man have always been
in each other's faces.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.420
Today they're in each other's bodies!"

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:38.980
"Oh my God!"

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:44.420
As Holland explained, Ultimate Spider-Man
#66 sees Peter waking up and not recognizing

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.590
anything in his house.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.180
In his hotel room, Wolverine is experiencing
the same confusion: he doesn't know who he

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:52.260
is and is startled by his appearance.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:56.000
While telling Mary Jane Watson that he really
doesn't want to go to school, Peter gets a

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.400
phone call from Wolverine.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.520
Their conversation leads to the big revelation:
they've swapped bodies.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:06.640
Peter and Wolverine meet at school, where
Wolverine (in Peter's body) is skipping class.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:11.020
When Peter and Wolverine are about to leave,
Peter (in Wolverine's body) heads toward a

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:15.360
car chase, which leads to an unfortunate event
involving an enormous truck.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:21.560
Ultimate Spider-Man #67 picks right up where
#66 left off, and follows Peter and Wolverine

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.200
as they try to figure out a way to reverse
the body swap.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.980
After a string of hilarious mishaps, fellow
X-Men member Jean Grey saves the day in a

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.300
hilarious twist.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.720
Holland's chat with Comics Explained caught
the attention of Brian Michael Bendis, the

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.680
writer behind the Peter Parker and Wolverine
body swap story.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:41.500
Bendis retweeted a video clip of the interview,
adding in the caption,

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.520
"EVERYone else can see this too, right?"

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.140
When it comes to a potential body swap movie
with Spider-Man and Wolverine, it isn't so

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:52.500
much a question of whether it can happen but
rather a case of whether Marvel Studios would

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.420
want to do it.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:58.580
Now that the Walt Disney Company owns the
majority of 20th Century Fox's assets, Wolverine

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:02.870
and the rest of the X-Men squad are property
of the Mouse House - and, more specifically,

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:03.680
Marvel Studios.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:07.750
Though Marvel's head honcho Kevin Feige has
mentioned that it will be "a handful of years"

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.349
before the Disney-Fox merger would impact
the MCU, he is looking to recast Wolverine

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:16.100
with a younger actor when the studio inevitably
reboots the X-Men team.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:21.670
It's only a matter of time before fans witness
a new Wolverine entering the MCU, where Holland's

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:23.520
Spider-Man is already a major player.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:28.180
Will the two cross paths and swap bodies for
a big-screen feature sometime in the future?

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.620
Never say never.

